Second Reality - Amiga OCS/ECS port, WHDLoad install
====================================================

Files:
  SecondReality.slave   WHDLoad slave
  disk.1, disk.2        the two disk images (same as the ADFs)

Start from a shell with:
  WHDLoad SecondReality.slave

or from any WHDLoad launcher.  No icon is included; to make one, copy any
WHDLoad project icon, name it SecondReality.info and set its tooltype
Slave=SecondReality.slave.

Requirements:
  - WHDLoad 10 or newer
  - 1 MB chip memory (the demo is written for 1 MB chip, OCS/ECS)
  - about 2.2 MB of other memory (both disk images are kept in memory, so
    the demo never waits for a disk, plus room for the 8 voice music)

Music (setting "Music" in the WHDLoad window, WHDLoad 17 or newer; or the
tooltype CUSTOM1):
  4 voices (Paula)          as on the floppy version (CUSTOM1=0, default)
  8 voices 16.5 kHz         all 8 voices of the original music, mixed by the
                            CPU (CUSTOM1=1): needs a fast CPU (PiStorm,
                            68040/060, fast 68030)
  8 voices 8.3 kHz          the same at a lower rate, for slower
                            accelerators (CUSTOM1=2)
Holding the left mouse button while the demo starts also selects 8 voices
at 16.5 kHz.  With 8 voices the mixer works from a copy of the samples in
fast memory (part of the memory the slave asks WHDLoad for).

Quit with F10 at any time (or the quit key set in WHDLoad); the demo also
returns to WHDLoad by itself after the end scroller.
